text = """ In an age of constant stimulation, where our phones buzz with every notification and streaming platforms beg for our attention, boredom has become something of a modern taboo. We treat it like an enemy to be eliminated rather than a state to be explored. But boredom, when allowed to breathe, has an unexpected power. It clears space. It invites reflection. And it might just be one of the most underrated catalysts for creativity, self-discovery, and peace of mind.

